I've come up with a new format for doing the TWiki translations, and I'd
*really* like everyone to take a look.

I know it's a bit burdensome in terms of markup, but I think it ends up
looking quite good.

I also put up a short Lovecraft story to explicate it:

<http://www.lojban.org/cgi-bin/twiki/view/Translations/TheBook>

The new markup rules are linked from the main Tranlations TWiki page
<http://www.lojban.org/cgi-bin/twiki/view/Translations/WebHome>, and are
at
<http://www.lojban.org/cgi-bin/twiki/view/Translations/TranslationStyleAndMarkup>.

There is also a page for translation of the lojban.org front page into
other languages at
<http://www.lojban.org/cgi-bin/twiki/view/Translations/Lojbanorg>

Comments welcome.

Actual work translating even more welcome.  :-)

Also, feel free to add your own stuff!  The front page *is* editable.

